 "content": "# Continual-ARC observation: task-6e926b58

Observed rule from one demo (9x27 input -> 9x13 output) and a solved test (5x11 -> 5x5): input consists of two equal-width pattern panels separated by a one-cell-wide vertical divider. The divider is color 5 in the demo and color 1 in the test. In the demo, the left panel is 13 columns wide and contains color 3; the right panel is 13 columns wide and contains color 9. Output is a single panel of the same height/width as either side. Place output color 2 at each coordinate where the left panel has 3 AND the corresponding right-panel coordinate has 9; all other output cells are 0. The solved test confirms the analogous rule: left 5x5 panel color 6, right 5x5 panel color 5, divider color 1; output color 2 at the coordinate-wise intersection of 6s and 5s.

Reusable procedure: locate the vertical separator and split into equal-width panels; identify each panel's salient nonzero color; scan aligned coordinates and mark only cells where both panels have their salient colors, outputting 2 there and 0 elsewhere. Preserve height and panel width. Distinguish this intersection rule from copying one marker pattern alone."
